From a52f1cdd123fa84ab523171341909cbe467f003c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:46:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/29] CI: the suites could not fail the build; now they can,
 and their absence fails it too

set -o pipefail alone is not enough inside a { ... } group: the step's status is the last
command's, so tools/test/run_probe_tests.sh returning 1 in the middle of that block would have
left gradle to decide whether the run is green. Both suites were, in the useful sense, not wired in
at all - they were decoration. Reproduced locally in two lines: a failing first command of the
group exits 0 without -e and 1 with it.

Then the part that keeps this from regressing quietly: an 'Assert the test suites ran' step greps
the tee'd build log for each suite's own verdict line (all probe cases passed / declarations
checked / all adapter cases passed) and exits 1 if any is missing. A green job now means the probe
suite, the real-header ABI check and the adapter suite each reached their last line - not merely
that assembleDebug worked. That distinction is the whole lesson of this branch: twice something here
passed while looking verified.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .github/workflows/gpu-guard-ci.yml | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/gpu-guard-ci.yml b/.github/workflows/gpu-guard-ci.yml
index a20dae0..78eab20 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/gpu-guard-ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/gpu-guard-ci.yml
@@ -39,7 +39,12 @@ jobs:
       - name: Build the patched app and guest preloads
         id: build
         run: |
-          set -o pipefail
+          # -e matters more here than it looks: inside a { ... } group the step's status is the LAST
+          # command's, so with only pipefail a red test suite in the middle of this block still
+          # leaves gradle to decide whether the run is green. Verified locally - a failing first
+          # command exits 0 without -e and 1 with it. The "Assert the test suites ran" step below is
+          # the belt to this pair of braces.
+          set -eo pipefail
           # Everything the step does goes into the log the next step publishes. An earlier run
           # died in one second, before the build, and published "(no build log)": the step that
           # failed was the one nobody could read. pipefail keeps the failure visible as a failure.
@@ -61,6 +66,22 @@ jobs:
             bash drivers/mali-g615/test/run_adapter_tests.sh
             bash tools/build_local.sh
           } 2>&1 | tee /tmp/droiddeck-build.log
+      # A green build is not evidence that tests ran; it is evidence that gradle succeeded. The
+      # suites above print their own verdicts, so their verdicts are looked for here, in the log the
+      # step wrote, and this run goes red if one of them ever stops being reached.
+      - name: Assert the test suites ran
+        run: |
+          set -e
+          for marker in 'all probe cases passed' 'declarations checked' 'all adapter cases passed'; do
+            if grep -q "$marker" /tmp/droiddeck-build.log; then
+              echo "ran: $marker"
+            else
+              echo "missing from the build log: $marker"
+              echo "the suite did not run, or failed before printing its verdict"
+              exit 1
+            fi
+          done
+
       # The machine working on this branch cannot download Actions logs, only talk to the API, so
       # on failure the log is published as a check run where it can be read back.
       - name: Publish the build log
